      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-98075",
      ":question/problem": "It is known that $37%$ of a population has blood type O$+$. Let the random variable $X$ represent the blood type of a randomly selected donor: $X = 1$ if the donor has blood type O$+$ and $X = 0$ if they don't. By modeling the situation as a Bernoulli trial, determine the expected value of $X$."
